WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.067
-Welcome back!
We're here with Jeff Goldblum.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.234
Um, we're getting to some music.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.267
You're musical.
-Okay.

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:06.400
-We have boys
about the same age.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.400
-Yeah.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.601
-And yours are still
doing piano.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.767
I'm so impressed.
-Why? Yours were and stopped?

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.567
-Mine -- No, they're not doing
anything.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:13.934
I mean...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.300
But do they --
Here's my question.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.234
We've gotten them things
like guitars and drum sets,

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:19.400
and they like messing around
a little bit, but they don't --

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.901
There's no magnetism towards it.

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.300
Did your kids have it, like,
when they first started playing?

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.734
-I don't know that they had
a magnetism toward it,

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:30.100
but we exposed them to it,
offered them lessons.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.934
The one went to Suzuki --
a Suzuki school.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.167
He did okay with that.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.734
And they have a good teacher --
Pippa.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:36.901
Excuse me, I'm a little gassy.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:40.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.100
But --
-Just keep us updated.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.334
-Yeah.
-You know.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.734
-I will. I will.

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:47.167
But Pippa is very good,
and they're playing pretty well.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.501
-Yeah.
-Yes, Charlie, the one that's 7,

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:50.834
is doing very well.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.200
She's very thrilled with him.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.701
He kind of plays by himself now.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.434
He's off and running.
He likes it.

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:57.801
I think he considers himself
as kind of a pianist.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:58.901
-And do you like hearing it?

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:00.634
Does it make you happy?
-Yes, it does.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:03.300
And I kind of facilitate,
and so does Emilie.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.734
He's practicing every day.
He practices every day.

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.367
That's what I missed out on
when I was a kid.

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:11.067
My mom didn't really
make me practice.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:13.601
Maybe she -- That's okay, but I
finally kind of got into it.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:16.467
Anyway, they're doing well.
I play a duet with Charlie.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:17.901
We do "The Band Played On."

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:20.501
♪ Da-da-da-da, da-da-da,
da-da-da ♪

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.000
It's cute, and we do it for
other people.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.300
We like to perform a little bit.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.067
River also plays very well.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.667
So they're doing okay.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.934
-That's wonderful. I'm happy.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.534
Yours must be doing many things.

00:01:30.534 --> 00:01:32.667
-They're doing many things,
but...

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:36.033
-[ Laughs ]
-Nothing where, like,

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.467
when you have friends over,
you're like,

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.501
"Wait till you get
a look at this," yeah.

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:42.100
-Well, it doesn't have to be.
It doesn't have to be.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.000
River actually has so much
confidence. I don't know why.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.467
He went -- He played piano,
but then he went, "Okay."

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:50.133
I said, "Hey, are you gonna tell
that joke?"

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.667
Because I'd told him a joke,
and then he kept repeating.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.434
And I said, "You want to tell
everybody?"

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.601
And he was like, "Okay. Okay."

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:57.634
And then he told a joke,

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:59.200
and then he said,
"Okay, wait, wait,"

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.267
and he started to go into
a snap routine

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.968
'cause he'd just learned
to snap his fingers,

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:05.934
which is a big
kind of rite of passage.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.567
And, anyway, he --
And then I joined in.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:08.601
We did a little of that.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.334
So...yours can do anything.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.634
It's not the -- It's not --
-Yeah.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.033
-It's they're qualified
if they just do it.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.234
-There you go.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.334
I wonder where he gets
his confidence, your son.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:20.767
-I seem to have confidence?

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:23.400
-You? I love -- Your energy is
one of my favorite energies

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.200
to be around --
everything about it.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.133
You're so comfortable
being Jeff Goldblum.

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.834
It's my favorite thing.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:31.033
Now, Mildred Snitzer --
The Mildred Snitzer Orchestra...

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.167
-Yes, sir.

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:33.534
-...we've talked about the name
before,

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:34.701
because you've obviously
been on the show.

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.400
Mildred Snitzer was
an actual person,

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.501
a friend of your mother's?

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:38.667
-In Pittsburgh,
where my dad is from.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:39.801
-Yeah, in The Burgh.
There you go.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.133
-We love The Burgh.
-We love The Burgh here.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:42.267
We love The Burgh.
-Love The Burgh.

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:44.067
The Steelers. Go Steelers.
-Yep.

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.601
-Yeah, Mildred Snitzer
was a lovely woman

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:49.400
who used to visit my mom,
and, you know.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.167
-Was she -- Did she ever live to
know that her name was --

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.434
-You know, funny you should ask.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:54.767
I don't think
I told anybody this,

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:58.734
but she lived, first of all,
to be about 102 or 104.

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:00.133
-Good for her.
-First of all.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:02.734
And, in her 80s, 90s --
We've been playing out and about

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:04.133
for the last 30 years.

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:06.434
We had a weekly gig someplace
in California at the time.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:07.501
We've moved around.

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:09.167
She was -- had moved
from Pittsburgh

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:12.167
to Northern California,
and one night --

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:14.734
I'll be darned -- John Mastro,
who was backstage, our manager,

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:16.000
said, "Guess who's here?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.667
Mildred Snitzer."
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:21.601
-And she -- she -- she waltzed
in with some kind of sequined --

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.901
She'd dressed up
for the occasion.

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.901
She was dancing around.
She was 80 or 90.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.167
Yeah. So she saw us.
How about that?

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:27.334
-Well, there you go.

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:28.934
And what song are you gonna
do first tonight?

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:31.434
-Ooh, we're going to do
a song...

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:34.501
[ Laughter ]
...that you know all too well.

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:36.067
Mattiel Brown --
the great Mattiel Brown --

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.501
is gonna sing it.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:41.534
It's been arranged by Joe Bagg,
our virtuoso organ player.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.434
And the name of the song is,
well, I'll give you a hint.

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:44.701
I'll bet you'll know it.

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:48.067
It's from -- It was sung
by Audrey Hepburn in a movie

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.067
called "Breakfast at Tiffany's."

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:52.100
[ Audience "Ooh"s ]
Of course, it's...

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.767
-"Moon River."
-"Moon River." There we go.

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:56.200
We got one. I knew it, so that's
the only reason I didn't say it.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.534
[ Laughter ]
-And the first --

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.367
And the first two bars
go like this.

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.367
Listen to this.

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.367
♪ Moon ♪

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:03.534
You're gonna sing with me.
-Okay.

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:07.734
-♪ Moon...river ♪

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:10.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.734
♪ Wider...than...a...♪

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.200
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.901
-Very good.
Hey, we're like Sandler &amp; Young.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:22.133
-We are like Sandler &amp; Young.
-You don't know Sandler &amp; Young.

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:23.734
-Adam Sandler and Burt Young.

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:25.267
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:27.167
-That's so good.
No, Adam Sandler --

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:29.801
Sandler &amp; Young were big
on "The Merv Griffin Show."

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.133
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.400
Alright, well,
you're sticking around.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.968
I can't believe my luck tonight.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.200
You guys, that's Jeff Goldblum.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.167
We're gonna be right back
with a performance --

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:39.133
Jeff Goldblum and
The Mildred Snitzer Orchestra.

